# =====================================================================
# FILE: .gitignore   -  "files Git should NOT upload"
# =====================================================================
# HOW TO READ THIS FILE
#   Lines starting with # are comments. Every other line is a pattern
#   naming files or folders that Git should ignore.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES, IN PLAIN ENGLISH
#   Git is the tool that records your project's history and uploads it to
#   GitHub. This file is a "do not pack" list: anything matching a line
#   below stays on your computer and is never uploaded.
#   Note: the file name starts with a dot, which hides it in some folder
#   views. That is normal.
# =====================================================================

# node_modules/ = the folder 'npm install' creates, holding the downloaded
# libraries (Express, sql.js and everything they need: thousands of
# files). WHY IGNORE IT: anyone can recreate it exactly by running
# 'npm install' (package-lock.json records the exact versions), so
# uploading it would only waste space. The trailing / means "a folder".
node_modules/

# data/*.db = any file ending in .db inside the data folder - i.e. the
# database file data/recruiter.db. The * means "any name".
# WHY IGNORE IT: it is created automatically from the SQL files the first
# time the server starts, and it changes every time you add test data.
# The SQL files (db/schema.sql, db/seed.sql) are the real source.
data/*.db
